---
import InformationLayout from '@/layouts/InformationLayout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '@/config/site';
---

<InformationLayout title="Privacy Policy" description="How the M.P. Public School website handles school enquiries, third-party services, device storage, and privacy requests." updated>
  <h2>Who this policy covers</h2>
  <p>This policy explains the information handled through the {siteConfig.name} website at <a href={siteConfig.url}>{siteConfig.url}</a>. School enquiries are directed to {siteConfig.fullName}, {siteConfig.address}. For privacy questions, contact <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.email}`}>{siteConfig.email}</a> or <a href={`tel:${siteConfig.phones[0].replace(/\s/g, '')}`}>{siteConfig.phones[0]}</a>.</p>

  <h2>Information you provide</h2>
  <p>The admission enquiry asks for a student name, parent or guardian name, phone number, email address, class of interest, and an optional message. The general enquiry asks for your name, phone number, optional email address, and message. We use these details to respond to the question and discuss the school services you ask about.</p>
  <p>Please provide only the information needed for your enquiry. The website forms do not request identity-document numbers, payment-card information, medical records, or document uploads. Formal admission records are handled separately through the school office.</p>

  <h2>Google Forms, WhatsApp, and other services</h2>
  <p>Submitting a website enquiry sends the entered details to the school's form hosted by Google Forms. Your browser then opens Google's response page. Google processes service and technical information under its <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Privacy Policy</a>. Submission does not create a website account or confirm admission.</p>
  <p>WhatsApp, email, telephone links, and social links open the corresponding third-party service or an app on your device. Information you send through those channels is also subject to that service's practices. Google Maps is embedded on the website; loading a map may share your IP address, browser information, and cookies with Google.</p>

  <h2>Website storage and technical information</h2>
  <p>The website uses a service worker and browser storage to cache resources and remember choices related to app installation and updates. Hosting services may process IP addresses, requested URLs, and browser details when serving pages. Browser settings let you clear site storage or block cookies; this can affect app and embedded-service features.</p>
  <p>This website build does not install Google Analytics, Google Ads conversion tracking, or remarketing tags. If tracking is added, this policy and any required consent controls must be updated to describe the actual use.</p>

  <h2>Access, sharing, and retention</h2>
  <p>Enquiry information is intended for school personnel handling your request and service providers involved in delivering it. Information may also need to be disclosed when required by applicable law. Contact the school before submitting if you need details about access to the enquiry records or their retention period.</p>
  <p>You can ask the school to correct or delete an enquiry, explain its use, or stop optional follow-up. Include enough information to identify your request without sending sensitive documents. Deletion may be limited where admission records or other information must be retained under applicable requirements.</p>

  <h2>Children and published school material</h2>
  <p>Admission enquiries should be submitted by a parent or guardian. The adult submitting a child's information should be authorised to do so. Student images, names, and results may appear in school-provided publications, including the school diary. Contact the office about permission, correction, or removal of a published item.</p>

  <h2>Contact and policy updates</h2>
  <p>Send privacy requests or concerns to <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.email}`}>{siteConfig.email}</a>, identifying the website page or enquiry concerned. Changes to this policy will be published on this page with an updated date.</p>
</InformationLayout>
